  "question": {
    "text": "As shown in the figure, two infinitely long, identical wires are bent by <math><msup><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> and placed in such a way that the segments <math><mi>L</mi><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi><mi>M</mi></math> are along the <math><mi>x</mi></math> - axis, while segments <math><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi><mi>N</mi></math> are parallel to the <math><mi>y</mi></math> - axis. If <math><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> and the magnitude of the magnetic field at <math><mi>O</mi></math> is <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo></math> and the two wires carry equal currents (see figure), the magnitude of the current in each wire and the direction of the magnetic field at <math><mi>O</mi></math> will be <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo></math><br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0186_b62cbcc3c846.png\" />"
  },
